No nuvem baseline for these keys. Here are my findings.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "supabase/config.toml",
    "line": 55,
    "summary": "Bucket table key with a hyphen ([storage.buckets.widget-assets]) is not a valid bare TOML key for the Supabase CLI bucket map.",
    "failure_scenario": "`supabase start` parses config.toml; the unquoted hyphenated key `widget-assets` either is rejected as an invalid bucket id (Supabase bucket ids/keys are validated) or fails TOML/decoding, so the storage seeding section errors out and the stack does not start. Should be quoted: [storage.buckets.\"widget-assets\"]."
  },
  {
    "file": "supabase/config.toml",
    "line": 52,
    "summary": "`objects_path` is the wrong field name for seeding a storage bucket; the CLI expects `objects_path` only in newer schemas — verify vs `public`/no-seed support.",
    "failure_scenario": "If the CLI version (v2.101) does not recognize `objects_path` under [storage.buckets.*], `supabase start` errors with an unknown-key decode failure, OR silently ignores it so the `ativos`/`widget-assets` buckets are created empty — widget-loader then fetches widget.js and gets 404, returning HTTP 500 to every Moodle page."
  },
  {
    "file": "supabase/config.toml",
    "line": 70,
    "summary": "`enable_signup` under top-level [auth] may be deprecated/renamed; modern CLI uses [auth] enable_signup but older/newer splits differ.",
    "failure_scenario": "If the CLI rejects `enable_signup` at the [auth] level (it lives under [auth] in current schema but was historically only valid there), an unknown-key error aborts `supabase start`. Lower risk than the buckets, but flagged for the targeted version."
  },
  {
    "file": "widget-src/build.mjs",
    "line": 90,
    "summary": "`__DARCY_VOICE_ENABLED__: String(VOICE_ENABLED)` injects the bare token `true`/`false` but config.ts declares it as `boolean` and assigns to VOICE_ENABLED — fine, EXCEPT if define is ever missing the identifier is undefined at runtime.",
    "failure_scenario": "If build.mjs is bypassed (e.g. someone runs esbuild without these defines, or a future entrypoint), `__DARCY_VOICE_ENABLED__` is an undeclared bare identifier → ReferenceError at widget load, breaking the whole widget. The `declare const` gives no runtime fallback. Same applies to the three JSON.stringify'd string globals."
  },
  {
    "file": "widget-src/build.mjs",
    "line": 19,
    "summary": "loadDotEnv strips only ONE leading/trailing quote and trims, but does not handle inline `#` comments or values; trailing-quote-only regex can mangle values.",
    "failure_scenario": "A .env line like `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=\"eyJ...\" # local key` keeps the ` # local key` suffix inside the value (no inline-comment stripping) AND the closing-quote regex `/^[\"']|[\"']$/g` only removes the very last char if it's a quote — here the last char is `y` (from comment), so the quote and comment are baked into the JWT, producing an invalid anon key → all widget/dashboard requests 401."
  },
  {
    "file": "widget-src/src/services/config.ts",
    "line": 18,
    "summary": "`SUPABASE_URL.replace(/^http/, 'ws')` is correct for http/https but silently produces a broken WS URL if SUPABASE_URL lacks an http scheme.",
    "failure_scenario": "If the tunnel URL is configured without scheme (e.g. `my-tunnel.ngrok.app`) the regex no-ops, so API_VOICE_WS = `my-tunnel.ngrok.app/functions/v1/darcy-voice` (no ws scheme) → WebSocket constructor throws SyntaxError, voice silently never connects. https→wss and http→ws cases are correct."
  },
  {
    "file": "supabase/functions/widget-loader/index.ts",
    "line": 11,
    "summary": "SUPABASE_URL inside the edge function resolves to the INTERNAL kong host (often kong:8000), and the public-object path built from it is fetched server-side — generally OK, but the localhost default is wrong inside Docker.",
    "failure_scenario": "If `SUPABASE_URL` is NOT injected (functions served standalone, or a runtime that doesn't set it), it falls back to `http://127.0.0.1:54321`, which from inside the edge_runtime container points at the container itself, not kong → fetch to /storage/v1/... fails/ECONNREFUSED → widget-loader returns 500, no widget served."
  },
  {
    "file": "supabase/config.toml",
    "line": 81,
    "summary": "`[edge_runtime] policy = \"oneshot\"` — valid values are typically `oneshot`/`per_worker`; confirm key spelling for v2.101 (some versions used different naming).",
    "failure_scenario": "If `policy` under [edge_runtime] is an unrecognized key in the targeted CLI schema, `supabase start` aborts on config decode. Lower confidence — `oneshot`/`per_worker` are the documented values — but flagged because an invalid enum/key here is fatal to startup."
  }
]
```

Two highest-confidence blockers: the unquoted hyphenated bucket key (line 55) and the brittle `loadDotEnv` quote/comment handling (line 19), which will silently corrupt JWT-style values. The `objects_path` field name (line 52) is the other key risk — if wrong/ignored, buckets seed empty and `widget-loader` 500s on every request.
